The otherwise valid DSSE bundle contains an in-toto statement with an unknown
_type value. Verification must not interpret unknown statement semantics as
https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1.

Creation: generate ECDSA P-256 artifact-signing and tlog keys; create a statement
whose SHA-256 subject is `../a.txt` and whose `_type` is
`https://in-toto.io/Statement/v2`; sign its PAE; and record the PAE digest and
signature in a hashedrekord/0.0.2 entry. The custom log has one leaf, so its
root is `SHA256(0x00 || canonicalizedBody)`; sign that checkpoint with the tlog
key and place its public key in `trusted_root.json`.
